Ours.  Declarations gcc 14 needs in the X server (dix, os, Xext, xkb, mi, the Amiga DDX):
each file that called a function with no declaration gets a prototype after its
includes, taken from the definition the call links with (gcc -aux-info).  A K&R
definition's narrow parameters are default-promoted in the prototype, as a K&R caller
passes them (char/short/their typedefs -> int, float -> double):
  programs/Xserver/Xext/security.c: RemoveAuthorization(short unsigned int name_length -> int); RemoveAuthorization(short unsigned int data_length -> int)
Declared without a prototype (types not defined at that point, or called with varying
arguments; none has an ANSI definition with a narrow parameter): ClientSleepUntil 
WriteSConnSetupPrefix XdmcpAllocARRAY8 XdmcpReallocARRAY16 XdmcpReallocARRAYofARRAY8 
XkbFilterEvents XkbFreeInfo XkbFreeSrvLedInfo XpUnsetFontResFunc 

